#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "CAP-ONBOARDING Tenant onboarding registry"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "One reviewed declaration per product or source generates its identities, grants, schemas and reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: delivery · depends on: [CAP-DELIVERY]{1}, [CAP-CATALOG]{2}, [CAP-CIIDENTITY]{3}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Adding a product or a data source comes down to one reviewed file, and everything it needs is generated from that file."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Identities and grants made by hand drift, and nobody removes them. With one declaration for each tenant, there's one place to review its access and one place to revoke it ([P5]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "A `tenants/<name>.yaml` file in the platform repository, giving the owner role, domain, ingestion method, highest classification, the catalogs written and read, the operational database and the trusted repository."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "What is generated from it: identities, federated credentials, grants, schemas and required reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Outputs published for each product and environment, which the product's pipeline uses."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "This is where the platform and a product divide. The platform owns anything that crosses a permission boundary, and the product owns whatever is inside its grant."
msgstr ""

