#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "CAP-ONBOARDING.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Each product or source has one tenant entry declaring its owner role, domain, ingestion method, highest classification, the catalogs it writes and reads, its operational database, and the repository the platform trusts for it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Every product's resources trace back to exactly one tenant entry."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "CAP-ONBOARDING.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Identities, grants, schemas and required reviewers are generated from the entry and never created by hand."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "A reconciliation diff between generated and live grants is empty."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "CAP-ONBOARDING.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "The platform publishes each product's outputs per environment (endpoints, catalog names, identities, compute IDs) to the product, and a product never reads platform state."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "The product's configuration takes these values from published outputs; it has no access to platform state."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "CAP-ONBOARDING.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Removing a tenant entry removes the access it generated."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-onboarding.md
msgid "Off-boarding test: remove an entry; its identities and grants are gone after apply."
msgstr ""

